{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "lib": ["ES2020"],
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "composite": true,
    "incremental": true,
    "types": ["node"],
    "paths": {
      "@rediacc/shared": ["./packages/shared/src/index"],
      "@rediacc/shared/*": ["./packages/shared/src/*"]
    }
  },
  // NO `files` AND NO `include`, DELIBERATELY, and do NOT "fix" that -- it was tried and
  // reverted the same morning (b6e4ac65b, undone here).
  //
  // The temptation: with neither key, tsc treats this as matching EVERY .ts under the repo,
  // so a bare `npx tsc --noEmit` here compiles the whole tree under the options this file
  // exists to SHARE rather than apply -- lib ES2020, `types: ["node"]`, no DOM, no astro,
  // no workers-types -- and reports 10,095 errors that are all the wrong config and none of
  // them a defect. `"files": []` is the textbook solution-file fix and it silences that.
  //
  // WHY IT IS WRONG HERE. eslint lints type-aware through `projectService`
  // (eslint.config.js:312), which picks a file's project by walking UP to the nearest
  // tsconfig.json. Every `__tests__` tree is EXCLUDED by its own package's build config, so
  // for 356 files -- packages/cli/src/**/__tests__ (144), private/account/tests (94),
  // packages/shared/src/**/__tests__, packages/cli/scripts, private/account/scripts -- the
  // match-everything root IS the project of last resort. Add `files: []` and all 356 fail
  // to PARSE: "was not found by the project service", and `check:lint` reds in CI.
  //
  // So the cosmetic hazard stays. `npm run typecheck` is the supported way to check types
  // and runs each project under its own options; a bare `tsc` here is not a workflow
  // anybody has, and check:ci-typecheck-scope-coverage special-cases this file for exactly
  // this reason.
  "references": [
    { "path": "./packages/shared" },
    { "path": "./packages/cli" }
  ]
}
